SOAPBOX: Tried the dark side of the contests :)
SOAPBOX: Due to some daily activity with family, I've decided to try 80m.
SOAPBOX: I've expected more activity on
SOAPBOX: contest dedicated frequencies (3580/3590), but, around 0100z
SOAPBOX: everybody moved to 3573.
SOAPBOX: Saturday evening with preety high QRN due
SOAPBOX: to some local rain/thunderstorms around QTH (over 2h).
SOAPBOX: I was QRT around 2h prior daily light. some more QSOs were possible,
SOAPBOX: but I was too tired.
SOAPBOX: While lower bands are more atractive in CQ WW CW/SSB,
SOAPBOX: pointing on 80m resulted for a less activity
SOAPBOX:(40m was I guess more popular).
SOAPBOX: N1MM+ with WSJT-X worked almost without problem.
SOAPBOX: Guess, for some HAMs, the whole setup is pain in the ass :).
SOAPBOX: Normally, a contest log can be prepared in several seconds...
SOAPBOX: I've used YT video (on german) from Funkwelle to do it.
SOAPBOX: Thanks for the help!
SOAPBOX: ICOM 7600, power somewhere between 400 and 500w,
SOAPBOX: antenna spiderbeam 18m GP with 4 elevated radials.
SOAPBOX: Zik DK8ZZ
SOAPBOX: ps. CW/SSB contests still makes fun too :D
